    "created_at": "2019-07-18T18:29:34Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-07-18T18:33:21Z",
    "body": "I agree people can hack up something that is unintuitive and weird today. I don't think that's necessarily a great motivation for adding such semantics to the platform natively, especially if---as you explain---it's pretty easy to do without native support.\r\n\r\nI think we could make it even easier, while maintaining the current invariant that in-page scripts run in the page's process, via a new string API. So that your example would become\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<!doctype html>\r\n<html>\r\n<body>\r\n<canvas id='output' width='100' height='100'></canvas>\r\n<script id='myWorker' type='text/worker'>\r\n// wortker JS code\r\n</script>\r\n<script>\r\nvar worker = Worker.fromString(document.getElementById('myWorker').textContent);\r\n</script>\r\n</body>\r\n</html>\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis seems to strike a better balance to me.",
