    "created_at": "2020-04-30T12:07:13Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-04-30T12:07:13Z",
    "body": "I came across this issue while searching the tracker to see if someone proposed creating a Worker from Response before. @domenic's snippet looks pretty close to what I had in mind, but I was wondering if it would make more sense to add a Promise-based API similar to `WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming`:\r\n\r\n```js\r\nWorker.instantiate('...').then(worker => ...);\r\nWorker.instantiate(fetch('...')).then(worker => ...);\r\nWorker.instantiate(new Response('...')).then(worker => ...);\r\n```\r\n\r\nWith this, we could kill two birds with one stone and provide both a way to create workers from custom requests/responses, as well as a way to get load/error status in a unified way.",
